---
title: "One sticky note: typing, saving, outside edits, conflict versions, archive and Trash"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: editing
    lg1: syncing
    lg2: stored
    lg3: Breaks TypedTextKept or WindowMatchesDisk
    lg4: Breaks CloseAlwaysWorks or NoSpuriousConflictBlock in some cases
    lg5: Path to the CloseAlwaysWorks or NoSpuriousConflictBlock or TypedTextKept or WindowMatchesDisk bug
    state "Terms" as terms {
      direction TB
      state " " as tc0 {
        direction LR
        tm0: person = The owner, using Sticky Notes on this Mac.
        tm1: save timer = The half-second pause after typing before the note is written to its file.
        tm2: file watcher = The part of the app that notices the note's file changed on disk.
        tm3: desk = The app part that keeps one window per active note.
      }
      state " " as tc1 {
        direction LR
        tm4: outside edit = A change to the note's file made by Obsidian, the other Mac or iCloud.
        tm5: conflict version = A second copy of the file that iCloud keeps when two saves disagree.
        tm6: conflict sweep = The app step that merges conflict versions back into the file.
        tm7: other Mac = The owner's second Mac, used in turn, not at the same time.
      }
      state " " as tc2 {
        direction LR
        tm8: Obsidian = The notes app that shares the vault folder.
        tm9: iCloud = iCloud Drive, which syncs the vault between the Macs.
        tm10: placeholder = A hidden stand-in file iCloud leaves for a file it has not downloaded.
        tm11: archive = Closed notes, still listed in the notes panel.
      }
      state " " as tc3 {
        direction LR
        tm12: Trash = Notes deleted from the archive, kept 30 days.
      }
    }
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 orange
  class lg2 teal
  class lg3 breaks
  class lg4 mayBreak
  class lg5 bugPath
  s0: New note, no file yet
  s1: File changed, window not told yet
  s2: No note file, window closed
  s3: Typing, save pending
  s4: Save pending, person in another window
  s5: Outside edit held back
  s6: Note open, nothing pending
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s0: the person types in the note or the disk stops accepting writes
  s0 --> s1: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s1 --> s3: the person types in the note
  s0 --> s2: the person clicks the note's close button
  s3 --> s4: the person switches to another window
  s3 --> s3: the disk stops accepting writes
  s4 --> s4: the file watcher reports the change to the window [the window shows it] or the disk stops accepting writes
  s3 --> s1: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s1 --> s5: the file watcher reports the change to the window [the window holds it back]
  s5 --> s5: the disk accepts writes again
  s4 --> s6: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s3 --> s5: the file watcher reports the change to the window [the window holds it back]
  s5 --> s4: the person switches to another window
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
  class s0 teal
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 orange
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 teal
  class s2 breaks
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 orange
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 mayBreak
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 orange
  class s5 mayBreak
  class s5 bugPath
  class s6 blue
  class s6 breaks
  class s6 bugPath
